					      <div class="ecs-posts elementor-posts-container elementor-posts   elementor-grid elementor-posts--skin-custom" data-settings="{&quot;current_page&quot;:1,&quot;max_num_pages&quot;:999,&quot;load_method&quot;:&quot;numbers_and_prev_next&quot;,&quot;widget_id&quot;:&quot;c5573b4&quot;,&quot;post_id&quot;:51499,&quot;theme_id&quot;:51499,&quot;change_url&quot;:false,&quot;reinit_js&quot;:false}">
      		<article id="post-168094" class="elementor-post elementor-grid-item ecs-post-loop post-168094 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-uncategorized entry">
				<div data-elementor-type="loop" data-elementor-id="53239" class="elementor elementor-53239 post-168094 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-uncategorized entry" data-elementor-post-type="elementor_library">
					<section class="elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-533038e elementor-section-full_width elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default" data-id="533038e" data-element_type="section" data-e-type="section" data-settings="{&quot;background_background&quot;:&quot;classic&quot;}">
						<div class="elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default">
					<div class="elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-8880ea2" data-id="8880ea2" data-element_type="column" data-e-type="column">
			<div class="elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated">
						<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-8b6f3b3 elementor-widget elementor-widget-theme-post-title elementor-page-title elementor-widget-heading" data-id="8b6f3b3" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="theme-post-title.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h3 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default"><a href="https://www.dailypress.senate.gov/friday-november-20-2026/" target="_blank">Friday, November 20, 2026</a></h3>				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-60a5dd9 elementor-widget elementor-widget-theme-post-content" data-id="60a5dd9" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="theme-post-content.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">5:13 p.m. The Senate stands adjourned until 3:00 on Monday, November 30th with the exception of pro forma sessions on the following dates and times:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Tuesday, November 24th at 3:00 p.m. </li>



<li>Friday, November 27th at 12:00 noon</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">During wrap-up: </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The following resolutions were adopted en bloc by unanimous consent:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>S.Res.969 &#8211; Native American Heritage Month</li>



<li>S.Res.970 &#8211; Texas Southmost College 100 Years of Service</li>



<li>S.Res.971 &#8211; National First-Generation College Celebration Day</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">******</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">5:11 p.m. By a vote of 45-33, the Senate invoked cloture on the nomination of Jesus Osete to be United States District Judge for Western Missouri. This was a party-line vote with Senators Blackburn, Booker, Britt, Cassidy, Coons, Cornyn, Durbin, Gallego, Hickenlooper, King, Klobuchar, Lee, McConnell, Merkley, Moran, Murphy, Peters, Sanders, Shaheen, Tuberville, Warner and Whitehouse not voting. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">4:45 p.m. The Senate began a roll call vote on the motion to invoke cloture on the nomination of Jesus A. Osete to be United States District Judge for the Western District of Missouri. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">4:44 p.m. By a vote of 48 to 31, the Senate invoked cloture on the nomination of Peter Mansfield to be United States District Judge for the Eastern District of Louisiana.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Democrat Senators Fetterman and Hirono voted in favor.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Senators Blackburn, Booker, Britt, Cassidy, Coons, Cornyn, Durbin, Gallego, Hickenlooper, King, Klobuchar, Lee, McConnell, Merkley, Murphy, Peters, Sanders, Shaheen, Tuberville, and Whitehouse did not vote.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">4:34 p.m. The Senate is now voting on the motion to invoke cloture on Peter M. Mansfield to be United States District Judge for the Eastern District of Louisiana.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">4:33 p.m. By a party-line vote of 47-35, the Senate invoked cloture on Robert E. Long, Jr. to be United States District Judge for the Middle District of Florida. Senators not voting: Booker, Britt, Cassidy, Coons, Cornyn, Durbin, Hickenlooper, King, Klobuchar, McConnell, Murphy, Peters, Sanders, Shaheen, Tuberville, Warner, Whitehouse, and Wyden. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">4:19 p.m. The Senate began voting on the motion to invoke cloture on Robert E. Long, Jr. to be United States District Judge for the Middle District of Florida. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">4:17 p.m. Majority Leader Thune filed cloture on the following nominations. </p>



<ol class="wp-block-list">
<li>Executive Calendar #977, Robert E. Long, Jr. to be United States District Judge for the Middle District of Florida.</li>



<li>Executive Calendar #978, Peter M. Mansfield to be United States District Judge for the Eastern District of Louisiana.</li>



<li>Executive Calendar #979, Jesus A. Osete to be United States District Judge for the Western District of Missouri.</li>
</ol>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">4:16 p.m. By a vote of party-line 48-36, the Senate invoked cloture on Daniel Lewis Ballou to be United States District Judge for the Eastern District of Kentucky. Not voting: Blumenthal, Booker, Britt, Cassidy, Coons, Cornyn, Durbin, Hickenlooper, King, Klobuchar, McConnell, Murphy, Peters, Sanders, Tuberville, Warner. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">4:00 p.m. By a vote of 55-31, the Senate invoked cloture on Kyle Reardon to be a District Judge for the District of Alaska. Democrats voting aye: Cortez Masto, Fetterman, Hirono, Kaine, Rosen, and Shaheen. Senators not voting: Booker, Britt, Cassidy, Coons, Cornyn, Durbin, Hickenlooper, King, Klobuchar, Murphy, Padilla, Sanders, Tuberville, and Warner.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">3:37 p.m. The Senate began voting on the motion to invoke cloture on the nomination of Kyle Reardon to be a District Judge for the District of Alaska.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">3:35 p.m. Senator Barrasso locked in these votes following the cloture vote on the Reardon nomination:</p>



<ol class="wp-block-list">
<li>Motion to invoke cloture on Executive Calendar #967, Daniel Lewis Ballou, of Kentucky, to be United States District Judge for the Eastern District of Kentucky.</li>



<li>Motion to invoke cloture on Executive Calendar #977, Robert E. Long, Jr. to be United States District Judge for the Middle District of Florida.</li>



<li>Motion to invoke cloture on Executive Calendar #978, Peter M. Mansfield to be United States District Judge for the Eastern District of Louisiana.</li>



<li>Motion to invoke cloture on Executive Calendar #979, Jesus A. Osete to be United States District Judge for the Western District of Missouri.</li>
</ol>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">3:35 p.m. By a party-line vote of 49-41, the nomination of Courtney Coker to District Judge for the Northern District of Texas was confirmed.  Not voting: Senators Booker, Britt, Cassidy, Coons, Cornyn, Durbin, Klobuchar, Murphy, Tuberville, and Warner. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">2:45 p.m. The Senate began a roll call vote on the confirmation of Courtney Coker to be a District Judge for the Northern District of Texas.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">2:25 p.m. Senator Lankford spoke on permitting reform. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">1:45 p.m. Senator Moreno paid tribute to Fiona the Hippopotamus, who recently passed away at the Cincinnati Zoo. He then received unanimous consent to agree to S.Res.967 to honor Fiona the Hippopotamus and the Cincinnati Zoo staff. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">1:06 p.m. Senator Moran paid tribute to Amy France of the National Sorghum Producers</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">1:01 p.m. Senator Whitehouse thanked Senator Capito for her work on the permitting bill, and echoed her appreciation for staff and colleagues.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">12:43 p.m. Senator Capito thanked other members and staff for help on the permitting reform bill.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">12:42 p.m. By a party line vote of 49-43, the Senate invoked cloture on the nomination of Courtney Coker to be a District Judge for the Northern District of Texas. Not voting: Booker, Britt, Cassidy, Coons, Cornyn, Klobuchar, Murphy, and Tuberville.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">12:01 p.m. The Senate began a roll call vote on the motion to invoke cloture on the nomination of Courtney Leigh Coker to be United States District Judge for the Northern District of Texas. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">12:00 p.m. By a vote of 49-43, the Senate confirmed the nomination of Richard Wesley Bennett to be United States District Judge for the Southern District of Texas.</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>This was a party-line vote with Senators Booker, Britt, Cassidy, Coons, Cornyn, Klobuchar, Murphy, and Tuberville not voting. </li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">11:13 a.m. The Senate began voting on confirmation of Richard Bennett to be a District Judge for the Southern District of Texas.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">11:11 a.m. Senators Lankford and Murkowski paid tribute to Senator Armstrong.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">10:50 p.m. Senator Armstrong gave his farewell speech. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">10:33 a.m. Minority Leader Schumer spoke on Congressional oversight. He then spoke on Trump. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">10:23 a.m. Majority Leader Thune paid tribute to the military. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">10:04 a.m. Senator Grassley spoke about welfare reform. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">10:00 a.m. The Senate convened. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Senate will convene at 10:00 a.m. and following any Leader remarks will resume consideration of the nomination of Richard Bennett to be a District Judge for the Southern District of Texas.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">At 11:00 a.m., the Senate will proceed to two votes:<br>1. Confirmation of the Bennett nomination.<br>2. Cloture on the nomination of Courtney Coker to be a District Judge for the Northern District of Texas.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Further votes are expected, likely related to the following nominations, which have also had cloture petitions filed on them:</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">**Kyle Reardon to be a District Judge for the District of Alaska.<br>**Daniel Ballou to be a District Judge for the Eastern District of Kentucky.</p>
				</div>
				</div>
